hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21410","Abdullah said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to me, and this is the wording of Ibn Numayr's hadith, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yaqub from his father from Abu Hurayrah from Ubayy ibn Kab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down in the Torah nor in the Gospel the like of Umm al-Quran, and it is the seven oft-repeated, and it is divided between Me and My servant, and My servant shall have what he asks."
"21411","Abdullah said: Abu Mamar narrated to me, saying: Abu Usamah narrated to us from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Hurayrah from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you a surah, nothing like it was sent down in the Torah nor in the Zabur nor in the Gospel nor in the Quran. I said: Yes. He said: I hope I shall not leave that door until you know it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and I stood with him, and he took my hand and began speaking to me until he reached near the door. He said: So I reminded him and said: O Messenger of Allah, the surah you mentioned to me. He said: How do you recite when you stand to pray. So he recited Fatihat al-Kitab. He said: It is it, and it is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Quran which I was given afterwards."
"21412","Abdullah said: I asked my father, saying: Concerning al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman and Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, so he gave precedence to al-Ala over Suhayl, and said: I did not hear anyone mention al-Ala with evil. And Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Salih is more beloved to me than al-Ala."
